me was also a nod to japanese  animation disney released a copyright  document confirming that the name was a  play on porco rosso a film about an  italian pig pilot from the 90s aside  from japanese influence enrico also used  his love for looney tunes and took  inspiration from how the cartoon  demonstrated speed we'd have three you  know from my hand here to here to here  we would do all three of them to kind of  simulate quick speed even sean the sheep  had a part in luca in terms of how the  creators wanted to incorporate some  stop-motion vibes into the film as for  the creation of the sea monsters those  came from old renaissance maps from the  1500s and old italian sculptures they  found when they went to italy during  their pre-production research overall  enrico wanted these animations to be  unique and imperfect and even had the  computer make mistakes on purpose to  achieve his vision i love the sense that  all of our characters in some way feel  different or unusual luca's director put  his soul into the film literally the  story is loosely based on his experience  growing up in genoa with his best friend  alberto my best friend alberto was a bit  of a troublemaker alberto pushed me out  of my comfort zone and pushed me off  many cliffs metaphorically and not the  film's theme of friendship and being who  we are goes so much deeper than the  audience knows  i think he needs me  you know i can't do it without you while  the technical aspects faced many  challenges when it came to animations  the actors also faced difficulties  themselves luca is a part of the epic  collection of films that were made  during the covet 19 pandemic shout out  to raya and the last dragon the three  main characters luca alberto and julia  may have been the best of friends on  screen but off screen their actors  rarely saw one another because of  protocols some actors like jack dylan  grazer were forced to record their  voiceovers in their mom's closet  it's fine i'm not human  while he may have needed to have worked  around some sweaters and shoes his  makeshift studio seemed pretty cozy but  despite his unique studio the scenario  was still difficult for him it was  definitely a stretch for me a challenge  for me as an actor and as just a human  being not to mention he may have annoyed  his neighbors just a tad i bet my  neighbors were really freaked out about  the amount of screaming that was going  on from my house i don't know what they  were thinking as for jacob trombley who  voices luca he was a little luckier than  jack i actually started recording before  covet hit so i was able to go into the  san francisco studio and they gave me  the tour when the pandemic did arrive he  was prepared to get his closet turned  into a studio but instead was able to  safely record in a studio located in his  home city of vancouver  underdogs forever emma berman who played  julia didn't get a whole tour like jacob  but was lucky enough to record her part  in the studio as well look that's saturn  it's my favorite  they didn't get the full filming  experience but the cast still fell in  love with their characters and the story  of luca while jack and jacob just  couldn't get over how beautiful the  animation of the film turned out the  color of the sea and the sparkliness of  the sea emma fell in love and related  wholeheartedly to the character of julia  i had a really fun time playing her  because i relate to her in a lot of ways  we were both passionate about what we do  and we're also very excited and joyful  people alberto scorfano  you might think pixar's luca is just  another hit animated film but a look  behind the curtain reveals that it's not  just a movie about two teen sea monsters  it's so much more it's a motion picture  that shows us years of historical  italian legends and personal experiences  from the director himself that all led  to the true meaning behind luca ready to  find out what that meaning is  luca is yet another historical moment  for disney and pixar it's their first  film ever to solely focus on italian  culture and heritage as you can imagine  that means a lot of what we see  transpire to luca and alberto as well as  the setting has a real-life basis sure  porto rosso isn't a real italian town  however it's a near replica of the  italian fishing towns located in the  italian riviera as for the sea monsters  they exist too at least in the legends  of the italian people everyone portray  pretends to believe in sea monsters when  talking about the inspiration behind the  sea monsters director enrico casorosa  said there's a big history of sea  dragons for example one is in san  frutozo which has the famous abbey  it's a beautiful place that we  definitely took a lot of reference from  a place that is known for a dragon that  lives there along with the sea dragons  there were stories of friendly octopuses  and feisty krakens that even had  references in the film kind of sounds  interesting when it came to designing  the sea monsters they pulled out old  italian sea maps and took reference of  their illustrations however they did  have to tone down those illustrations a  little when they saw it become  overpowering in the film enrico said in  the beginning we were drawing them  really fantastical we were fascinated by  all these fins and all this weird and  kind of decorative elements on them in  the c-maps but it was like no they're  attracting too much attention to  themselves things like the fins on the  fish and the variety between them all  came from those old historical items  according to production designer daniela  strichlava they wanted to make sure they  kept the inspiration from the maps but  also be sure they were able to modify  them in order to fit each sea monster's  personality or home  the filmmakers even made sure that their  underwater scenes were in line with the  aquatic life in the mediterranean waters  and more specifically ligurian sea  isn't it great  plenty of research and personal  experience went into the making of the  film and luca as a character in fact  luca and alberto are loosely based on a  friendship enrico had while growing up  in italy he credits his past bff for  helping him come out of his shell and  get him where he is today his family  wasn't very present he couldn't do  whatever he wanted it was the perfect  friendship to get me out of my comfort  zone and help me grow up  what does that mean  no idea go find out for me will ya  the location was also chosen based on  enrico's childhood the director would  visit the italian riviera during the  summer months and his fond memories of  the towns were the reason for the  setting of lucca but of course enrico  couldn't rely on solely his own memories  to create a movie on italian culture who  wants to watch me eat a big sandwich  although he was raised there he spent  the majority of his adult life in  america that being said he put together  a team of art designers and sent them on  a mission to italy where they were  tasked with getting to know the culture  food and art in the country eriksen  thinks it's so important to get the  feeling of the place the light and the  details it has so much history the goal  visually of creating luca was to be able  to transport people to this beautiful  place that you would love to visit for  real but that you can visit through luca  that's how we're gonna see the world  [Music]  overall the goal of luca was to portray  the epic bonds of friendship enrico  wanted to make sure that the movie's  main symbolism of the importance of  friendship was at the forefront and not  sacrificed for added drama they even cut  certain scenes to make sure they kept it  in line with the vision we had much more  of a quest and we had a huge kraken  transformation at the end a big monster  finish we realized that wasn't the story  we wanted to tell all in all he was  going for a stand by me in italy vibe  luca represented the confusing and  challenging times we all experience when  we're 13. the frustration of not  identifying with your true self or  unsure how to express who you want to be  to others luca disguising himself was  actually a metaphor for that situation  and another extension of enrico's  personal experience  life is so much cooler than mine those  years where you feel odd in your own  body and you don't fit in for many  different reasons so something felt  right talking about that age with the  setting of a changeling someone actually  hiding his true self naturally because  he has to the contrast between the murky  ocean waters and wide and never-ending  human lands also helped showcase the  cramped feeling luca was experiencing as  a sea monster you just sit on it and it  takes you anywhere you want to go then  they were able to tie in the iconic  italian vespa to represent the freedom  luca had as a human fespa is freedom the  art team's research and enrico's  personal experience definitely paid off  they created a film that not only gave  representation to the beautiful italian  culture but a film about friendship and  growing pains that people around the  world can relate to what did you love  about luca thanks for watching
 

